# The HUD's cell voltage: Battery Cell Voltage on the HUD's menu asks "Cell Count", starting at 4,
# and the HUD then draws "Cell" and the pack's voltage over the count on the lower text line, the
# pack's own line moved up one; clicked again it turns the line off without asking. A count of 0
# draws nothing. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:6229-6254, ExtLibs/Controls/HUD.cs:2898-2925`
#
# Depends on fly.rs enabling the menu entry (fly-hud-batterycells) and porting its InputBox, which
# another change carries; until then the menu entry is dimmed and this fails at the prompt. The
# line's text and place for every count are proved by the unit tests in crates/mp-gui/src/hud.rs.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760, disarmed and at rest: SITL's pack reads 12.6 V with no
# current drawn (SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE), so four cells are 3.15 V, and there is no second battery.
# Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/hud-cells.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 5

# Off, as CheckBatteryShow leaves it with nothing saved: the pack alone on the lower line.
expect hud.battery.upper none
expect hud.battery.lower ~ Bat1 12.

# On, with the count the prompt starts at.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-batterycells
expect fly.prompt Cell Count
expect fly.prompt.value 4
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect hud.battery.lower ~ Cell 3.1
expect hud.battery.upper ~ Bat1 12.

# Clicked again: off, without a question.
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-batterycells
expect fly.prompt none
expect hud.battery.upper none
expect hud.battery.lower ~ Bat1 12.
